 "applies_to": "Greystone CR3 series cleanroom and critical-room monitors measuring temperature, humidity and room differential pressure, with BACnet MS/TP.",
 "summary": "The CR3 is a Greystone room monitor that measures temperature, RH and room differential pressure and talks native BACnet MS/TP. Nine Analog Inputs give the readings and their min/max values; Analog Values hold the low/high alarm setpoints, their allowed ranges, hysteresis and delays; Binary Inputs carry the six alarm states; Binary and Multi-State Values set units, display, outputs, alarms and menu locks.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "1.05 (PICS, August 16, 2021)",
 "default_device_instance": 381003,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Points from the object summary table on pages 2-3 of the setup guide.",
  "Temperature objects follow BV 1 (°C or °F) and pressure objects follow BV 2 (Pa or mmWc).",
  "Each alarm setpoint must sit between its Min and Max limit AVs; the limits themselves must stay a minimum span apart (e.g. 4 °C for temperature).",
  "Alarms do nothing until MV 1-3 enable them; by default only the DP alarms (MV 3 = Both) are on.",
  "Multistate objects are Multi-State Values (MSV) in the guide; listed here as MV. Access from the PICS: AV, BV and MSV Present_Value are writable."
 ],
